        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: வடிவமை",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "வடிவமை — vaṭivamai — \"to design\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "என் அக்கா இந்த வீட்டை வடிவமைத்தாள். eṉ akkā inta vīṭṭai vaṭivamaittāḷ. My elder sister designed this house."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): வடிவமைத்தேன், vaṭivamaittēṉ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The thing designed takes -ஐ. A designer is a வடிவமைப்பாளர்."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "வடிவமை (vaṭivamai) is a native compound: வடிவம் (vaṭivam), \"form, shape\" (DEDR 5223), and அமை (amai), \"to arrange, to fit together\" (DEDR 162)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
